# Both Dockerfiles do a bare `COPY apps/<x> /app`, so without this file the
# build context includes the host's node_modules and virtualenvs. That is
# not just slow (~580MB): node_modules and .venv contain platform-native
# binaries, so building on macOS or Windows would copy darwin/win32
# binaries into a Linux image and break the build or the runtime.
# The images install their own dependencies; never ship the host's.

# --- dependencies / build output (platform-specific, must not be copied) ---
**/node_modules
**/.next
**/out
**/.venv
**/venv
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/.mypy_cache
**/.pytest_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/*.egg-info

# --- secrets: never bake a real .env into an image layer ---
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# --- vcs / editor / os noise ---
.git
.gitignore
.github
**/.DS_Store
**/.idea
**/.vscode

# --- not needed at runtime ---
docs
**/*.md
apps/api/tests
apps/api/.coverage
apps/api/htmlcov
